# The BPE vocabulary depends on the exact bytes of the corpus: the shipped
# sample yields 308 ids with LF line endings and 310 with CRLF. With the
# default core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout would silently rewrite the
# corpus and produce a different tokenizer than a Linux clone.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths, so every platform
# checks out byte-identical data and prepare_data.py is reproducible.
data/raw/train.txt -text
data/processed/** -text
data/tokenizer.json -text
